* OPA161x_CUSTOM.lib -- LTspice-native behavioral approximation
* Independently created from TI OPA1611/OPA1612 datasheet SBOS450C.
* NOT a TI transistor-level model. NOT validated for THD+N, noise,
* PSRR, CMRR, overvoltage, thermal behavior, or power efficiency.
*
* One channel of OPA1611/OPA1612, with supplies in ANY orientation
* as long as VCC > VEE and total supply = 4.5V .. 36V.
* SPICE PIN ORDER: IN+  IN-  VCC  VEE  OUT
*
* Approximate datasheet characteristics:
* DC open-loop gain: 130dB (3.1623e6 V/V)
* Unity-gain bandwidth: 40MHz; dominant-pole single-pole model
* Slew rate: 27V/us; input bias current: +60nA each input
* Input offset voltage: +100uV; quiescent current: 3.6mA
* Input impedance: differential 20k||8p; common-mode 1G||2p
* Output swing: 0.6V from rails (conservative 2k load)
* Output drive: +55mA/-62mA; simplified output resistance 2ohm
*
.SUBCKT OPA161x INP INM VCC VEE OUT
*
* Floating local midpoint; neither supply is assumed to be GND.
BMID MID VEE V={0.5*V(VCC,VEE)}
*
* Input impedance and bias currents (illustrative nominal values)
RDIFF INP INM 20k
CDIFF INP INM 8p
RCMP INP MID 1G
RCMM INM MID 1G
CCMP INP MID 2p
CCMM INM MID 2p
IBP INP VEE 60n
IBM INM VEE 60n
*
* Dominant-pole open-loop stage: gm=1mS, R=3.1623G, C=3.979pF
* gm*R=3.1623e6 (130dB); gm/(2*pi*C)=40MHz
* 107.4uA / 3.979pF = 27 V/us, nominal slew rate.
BGM MID NAMP I={limit(1m*(V(INP,INM)+100u),-107.4u,107.4u)}
RDOM NAMP MID 3.1623G
CDOM NAMP MID 3.979p
*
* Restrict commanded output to a nominal range inside both rails.
* Headroom is a simplification and does not model load dependence.
BCMD NDRV VEE V={limit(V(NAMP),V(VEE)+0.6,V(VCC)-0.6)-V(VEE)}
*
* Output stage, current limited, approximated as 2-ohm driver.
BDRIVE NDRV OUT I={limit((V(NDRV,OUT))/2,-62m,55m)}
RBLEED OUT VEE 1G
COUT OUT VEE 2p
*
* Nominal (constant) supply current for a single channel.
IQ VCC VEE 3.6m
*
.ENDS OPA161x
